<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.360
<i>We've found a boat adrift.</i>

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.860
<i>It must be the research vessel
that was reported missing. Over.</i>

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.580
Hey, see anyone?

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.940
No. Nobody.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.070
What is this?

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.640
Hey!

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:58.220
Wh-What's going on?!

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.680
CHAPTER 58

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:12.710
THE HAN-GYOJIN'S STRANGE <i>KAMABOKO</i> TALE

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.410
Excuse me...

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.490
I'd like to ask about...

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.660
the accidents at sea...

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.680
Everyone's terrified.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.200
KAMABOKO

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.340
What a horrible sound.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:20.150
KAMABOKO

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.410
The water's great.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:32.750
I should bring some home for Dad.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:37.250
Whoops. I'm not here for leisure.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:43.010
Four ships have run into
similar accidents around here.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.560
According to one who barely survived...

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.510
A-A monster!

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:51.520
A monster did it!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.020
It might be <i>yokai</i>-related.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.520
At this rate...

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.680
Ah, I'm all warmed up.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:13.040
Oh! Kitaro-chan, what a coincidence!

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:15.040
You...

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:21.050
You're not involved with
these accidents are you?

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:24.630
Oh come on. I'm just a traveler.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:30.200
Driven by the winds of nostalgia, I'm
hiking to see the unspoilt land of Japan.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.960
Do you know anything?

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.000
Well, kind of...

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:45.400
Why are you taking me here?

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:49.030
Is there something here?

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.580
Now, now, now...

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.870
Hmm. A little to the right?

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.890
Okay, two steps right!

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:57.500
Good! Right there!

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.500
The perfect spot!

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:01.210
Hey...

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:07.850
What is this?!

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:11.050
Don't you know? You're so uneducated.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.310
It's called a giant squid.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.210
Well done, Rat Man!

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:23.320
HAN-GYOJIN

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.240
Han-Gyojin?!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.950
My business plan was about to be ruined.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:35.120
"Our"! "Our" business plan, right?

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:39.420
Rat Man! What are you up to?!

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.130
Now, now. Calm down.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:47.220
You're going to be
helping that business plan now.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.300
What?

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:53.530
<i>Han-gyo gyon gyon... Ka!</i>

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:09.930
This is...?

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:20.310
Wh-What is this?!

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:26.220
Observe! The power of Deep-Sea Witchcraft!

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.820
Hey, Han-Gyojin!

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.180
Turn me back!

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:33.090
Sadly, I don't have such abilities.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.640
It's your Deep-Sea Witchcraft!

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.140
How did you know?!

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.600
You just said so.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.980
Whoops. I spoke out loud.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:43.570
Come on. There's no need to play dumb.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:44.610
True.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.110
Okay, Kitaro, fetch me 100 tons of fish!

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.360
100 tons?!

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:54.700
I'm in the business of selling <i>kamaboko</i>.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:59.670
I had my pet giant squid gather
the fish needed to make it,

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.920
but it's rather dim-witted.

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:07.420
It started sinking ships
without my asking it to.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.170
Things were getting out of hand.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:12.550
That's when I thought,

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:18.930
I'd use my Deep-Sea Witchcraft
to make someone smart be its brains.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:24.790
You're an ocean-dwelling <i>yokai</i>.
What do you need money for?

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:28.690
That's not your concern.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.320
Now let's make a deal.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:35.510
Gather 100 tons, no, 200 tons of fish,
and I'll turn you back.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:39.350
Otherwise, you can be a squid forever.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.520
I'll do it. 200 tons, right?

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:46.540
It's a deal then!

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:47.920
SORRY, SOLD OUT

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:54.130
SOLD OUT

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.480
Isn't that enough?

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:05.520
No way. It isn't even half.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.150
Really?

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.340
Get some bigger ones.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.530
You're my slave forever.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:18.530
SOLD OUT

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:19.530
RESTOCKED

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.180
SOLD OUT

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.440
How many days has it been?

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:32.190
How many more fish do I have to catch?

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:36.050
I wonder if everyone in the forest's okay.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.180
What?

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.470
Kitaro?

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:05.310
Dad...

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.920
Ooh. You're in bad shape.

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:15.880
You're useless now. Oh well.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:20.280
<i>Han-gyo gyon gyon gyon gyon gyon gyon...</i>

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:23.600
Deep-Sea Witchcraft!

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:37.610
GETTING ALONG WITH A WHALE

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:42.120
HAN-GYOJIN

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.010
-<i>"Bottom's up!"</i>
-<i>"Let's do it!"</i>

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:42.010
<i>"Cheers!!"</i>

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.330
LIMITED FLAVOR

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:44.750
KITARO <i>KAMABOKO</i>

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:46.160
ONLY 100 AVAILABLE
100,000 YEN EACH

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.790
Hey, Han-Gyojin!

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:51.190
What's the meaning of this?!

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.800
Don't waste a single scrap.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:57.670
That's being eco-friendly.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.580
How could you?!

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.740
On... On...

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:08.850
Online sales was my department!

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.670
Huh? That?

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:16.530
I've learned all I need to about
online marketing.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:19.970
From now on I'll be handling everything.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:23.410
Ratty, you're fired.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:46.560
Oh no!

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:53.070
What?! Kitaro's been
turned into a <i>kamaboko</i>?

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:56.110
Wh-What do we do?! What do we do?!

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.280
Calm down, Catchick!

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:04.130
If we can get all of him,
we might be able to restore him!

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:07.660
Buy up those <i>kamaboko</i> right away!

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:09.910
They're 100,000 yen apiece!

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:14.420
How much do you think
buying all of them will cost?!

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:18.210
One... Ten... Hundred...

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:26.030
Ten million yen...

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:28.830
BANK BOOK

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:28.930
I'll pay for it.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:32.310
PURCHASE

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:39.530
Stocks, real estate,
Chobitcoin, tax havens...

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:43.950
Asset management is basic knowledge
for modern elders.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:48.330
C-Could you teach me some time?!

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.460
What an ordeal.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:03.140
The Yokai Hospital?

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:04.300
Indeed.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:09.180
I believe Kitaro could be restored there.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:15.310
There's a skilled doctor who's said to
even be able to resurrect the dead.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:20.110
However, the operating fee is
unbelievably high.

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:24.360
High? How many tens of thousands?

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.110
About 100 million.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.870
No way!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.500
Oh man...

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:33.250
I doubt even Sand Witch has that much...

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:34.370
BANK BOOK

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:36.100
I do.

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:44.920
HAN-GYOJIN

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:49.010
<i>Alkaline Yuriko of the popular idol group,
The Batteries,</i>

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.310
<i>announced her engagement on her blog.</i>

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:54.850
<i>Her partner is the investor,
Tsubasa Yokoizawa.</i>

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:59.670
<i>Their age difference of 26 years
is drawing attention.</i>

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:07.360
Unlike in the <i>yokai</i> world, in the human
world, those with money are important.

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:12.500
I may only be able to use
silly witchcraft,

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:16.770
but in this human world,
I can reach the top!

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:29.870
KAMABOKO

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:36.680
Hooray for the human world!

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.250
Han-Gyo.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.250
PRESIDENTIAL SEAL

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:43.710
Master, there's someone here
for the maid job interview.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:45.240
Bring them.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:46.420
Yes, sir.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:53.450
One million a month.
But, one speck of dust and you're fired.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:56.870
Appear in three seconds when summoned
or you're fired.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:15:01.190
No days off,
be it for a fever or death in the family.

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:18.750
I'm gonna catch you!

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.640
Um, is something the matter?

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:34.410
Marry me.

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.910
Excuse me?

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:37.910
I've got money!

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:39.460
You must be joking.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:40.770
Not enough?

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:43.790
Still not enough?

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:45.790
Boom! And boom!

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.550
Baboom and boom!

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:53.140
I appreciate the offer, but...

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:54.390
Why?!

00:15:55.330 --> 00:16:00.980
I'm a human and you're a <i>yokai</i>.
We can't be married.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:13.430
You wish to become a human?

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:16.990
Yeah!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:23.880
I hear you can even bring back the dead
if the money's right.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:26.480
I've got more than enough money!

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:28.210
It's irreversible.

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:35.090
Once made human,
you can't become a <i>yokai</i> again.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.370
Are you sure?

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:42.120
Dammit! Just get it over with!

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:54.360
I'm home!

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:56.490
Oh my!

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:59.560
What happened to you?

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:04.500
Now there's nothing to stand between us.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:07.210
For me...?!

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:11.650
Now marry me! Right now!

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:28.290
Wh-What's so funny?

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:34.240
"Once made human,
you can't become a <i>yokai</i> again."

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.430
Huh?! Where did you hear that?!

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:45.410
Y-You!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:47.920
I turned you into a <i>kamaboko</i>!

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:53.920
I was restored at the Yokai Hospital
you're familiar with.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:58.430
Curse you!
Maximum Deep-Sea Witchcraft!

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:01.430
<i>Han-gyo gyon gyon... </i>Boom!

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:07.020
Oh no! I'm not a <i>yokai</i> anymore!

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:15.780
Wait, let's talk this over!
I'm just a helpless human now!

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:19.720
No bullying the weak!

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:46.520
Screw you! I've got no attachment
to the <i>yokai</i> world!

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:50.770
I'm gonna enjoy my entertaining life
in this human world!

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:56.780
But will it be that easy?

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:01.140
Seriously?

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:02.470
Disgusting!

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:06.540
<i>A famous </i>kamaboko<i> business is</i>
<i>under heavy fire.</i>

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:10.090
<i>With photos posted by
a worker to social media,</i>

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:13.860
<i>people are questioning
the factory's management system.</i>

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:19.880
I'm from Mitsuboshi Bank.
I'd like to talk about your loan.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:22.780
<i>"I feel sick."</i>

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:25.020
Wh-What?! You're cancelling my loan?

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:24.540
-<i>"Return my money!"</i>
-<i>"Go under."</i>

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:29.350
How dare you!
You said, "borrow as much as you like!"

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:32.770
You only talk nice when it's convenient!

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:35.500
You want me to hang myself?!

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:41.740
You can hang yourself
after you pay us back.

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:45.990
This... This can't be happening!

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:53.710
<i>Alkaline Yuriko of the popular idol group,
The Batteries,</i>

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.440
<i>announced on her blog
she was breaking off her engagement.</i>

00:19:57.030 --> 00:19:59.010
<i>With her partner, Tsubasa Yokoizawa,</i>

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:04.320
<i>just having bombed in the </i>kamaboko<i> market,</i>
<i>the timing of this announcement is...</i>

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:33.920
I want to be a <i>yokai</i> again!

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:39.590
Didn't you love a world
where money is everything?

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:44.910
You can struggle to survive in
that cruel world.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.780
As a human.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:57.980
Thank you, Sand Witch.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:04.240
We're sorry for using up
so much of your savings this time.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:09.490
It's fine. When you have it it's useful,
when not, you get by.

00:21:09.770 --> 00:21:12.100
That's all that money is.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:15.120
Where's Rat Man?

00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:17.000
He's not here.

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:21.360
Honestly! Where is he hiding?

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:28.180
Despite all she says,
she's still concerned for Rat Man.

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:30.910
She probably just wants to hunt him.

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:37.210
I can't go back for a while.

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:43.050
I better fish to fight off the hunger
until things blow over.

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:45.900
Someone's already here.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.620
So, catching much here?

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:50.910
It's not bad.

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:17.750
<i>You're a dream
My dream</i>

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:17.750
<i>kimi wa yume boku no yume</i>

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:21.210
<i>I'm dreaming in a dream</i>

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:21.210
<i>yume no naka de yume miteiru</i>

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:24.720
<i>Let's stay like this forever</i>

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:24.720
<i>itsumade mo kono mama de imashou</i>

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:28.300
<i>You blur and begin to fade</i>

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:28.300
<i>kasuka kimi ga nijimu</i>

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:35.020
<i>Don't you cry
Where did you come from?</i>

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:35.020
<i>Don't you cry anata wa doko kara kitano?</i>

00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:39.770
<i>A masquerade
Faceless faces laugh</i>

00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:39.770
<i>kamenbutou kao no nai kao ga warau</i>

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>Hee-hee-hee</i>

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>fufufu</i>

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:45.820
<i>In dreams, in dreams
Lost in dreams</i>

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:45.820
<i>yume ni yume ni yume ni samayoi</i>

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:48.160
<i>Twirling around</i>

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:48.160
<i>kuru kuru to mawaru</i>

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:52.490
<i>Everyone dancing, dancing
Looking for love</i>

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:52.490
<i>dare mo odoru odoru ai wo sagashite</i>

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:59.330
<i>RONDO, spin, spin
Dream, dream</i>

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:59.330
<i>RONDO mawareyo maware yume yume</i>

00:23:01.540 --> 00:23:04.710
<i>Dad, humans are going missing.</i>

00:23:04.840 --> 00:23:07.590
<i>The common factor is... a cactus?</i>

00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:10.430
<i>Next time on GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:23:10.550 --> 00:23:13.100
<i>"Promise to The Female </i>Yokai
<i>Ushirogami"</i>

